@startuml
actor Customer
participant "React storefront" as UI
participant "Express REST API" as API
database PostgreSQL as DB
participant "Operations Portal (SSE)" as Ops

Customer -> UI : choose available product and quantity
UI -> API : GET /api/v1/products/catalog
API -> DB : read ONLINE machines and unexpired batches
DB --> API : available catalog
API --> UI : catalog + price + available stock

loop once for each item in basket
  UI -> API : POST /api/v1/transactions {machineId,columnId}
  API -> DB : validate machine, product and stock
  API -> DB : create PENDING transaction at server price
  DB --> API : transaction ID and authoritative amount
  API --> UI : transaction
  UI -> API : POST /transactions/{id}/simulate-payment SUCCESS
  API -> DB : conditional PENDING -> SUCCESS
  API --> UI : demo payment accepted
  UI -> API : POST /transactions/{id}/simulate-dispense SUCCESS or JAMMED
  API -> DB : Serializable stock / dispense update
  DB --> API : final simulated status
  API --> UI : result
  API --> Ops : transaction event via SSE
end

UI --> Customer : demo receipt and delivered / jammed item IDs
note over Customer,DB
No external payment provider or physical dispenser is called.
JAMMED requires staff/refund handling outside this demo.
end note
@enduml
